In a discussion initiated by user James, he asked about converting 10 Brazilian reais to PPP-equivalent terms. I explained the conversion process using PPP factors and discussed the implications of different GDP measurement methods: converting primero to USD and using the US deflator versus using national deflators first. James then sought guidance on categorizing GDP datasets, highlighting challenges with datasets that have varying interpretations. I suggested a structured spreadsheet with necessary columns for different GDP datasets and later refined this based on his specifications for full database-level records. Ultimately, we simplified the organization to focus on essential entries to facilitate empirical comparisons of the effects of different datasets on GDP per capita growth analyses.
